<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Puts a "ceremonial wardrobe owner" comp on Odyssey's outfit stands.

    MayRequire sits on the operations, not on a def: Building_OutfitStand's CLASS lives in
    Assembly-CSharp like all DLC code, so the mod's C# can name the type whether or not Odyssey
    is installed. Only the def is missing without it. That is what makes Odyssey a SOFT
    dependency here - without it the mod simply falls back to the no-building path.

    Two complementary operations rather than a match/nomatch pair. Patches run BEFORE def
    inheritance is resolved, so at patch time neither stand def carries a <comps> node of its own
    (they inherit one from OutfitStandBase). A single match/nomatch would only ever catch one
    half of the two defs; two predicates catch both, and neither errors on an empty match because
    each sits inside a PatchOperationConditional.

    THE SECOND PREDICATE HAS TO EXCLUDE OUR OWN li, and that is not decoration. Operations are
    applied in sequence to one accumulating document, so "has no comps" and "has comps" are not
    disjoint over time: the first operation CREATES the node that makes the second one's predicate
    true, and without the exclusion every stand ends up carrying the comp TWICE. Measured against
    Odyssey's real defs, both stands came out with two of them. Two comps of the same class on one
    building means two owner lists scribed under the same save key. Excluding the li also makes
    each operation idempotent, which is what lets them be read in any order.

    Adding a <comps> node to a def that inherits one is safe and is the intended way: XML
    inheritance APPENDS a child's <li> elements to the parent's list rather than replacing it.
    Ensuring the node exists rather than assuming it also keeps this def a commons - Shift Change
    and Outfit Stands Plus add comps to the very same def, and a def left with two <comps> nodes
    resolves last-wins with a red "defines the same field twice" error.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[(defName="Building_OutfitStand" or defName="Building_KidOutfitStand") and not(comps)]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[(defName="Building_OutfitStand" or defName="Building_KidOutfitStand") and not(comps)]</xpath>
      <value>
        <comps>
          <li Class="ForTheOccasion.CompProperties_AssignableToPawn_CeremonialStand" />
        </comps>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[(defName="Building_OutfitStand" or defName="Building_KidOutfitStand") and comps and not(comps/li[@Class='ForTheOccasion.CompProperties_AssignableToPawn_CeremonialStand'])]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[(defName="Building_OutfitStand" or defName="Building_KidOutfitStand") and comps and not(comps/li[@Class='ForTheOccasion.CompProperties_AssignableToPawn_CeremonialStand'])]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="ForTheOccasion.CompProperties_AssignableToPawn_CeremonialStand" />
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
